    "id": 14,
    "type": "todo",
    "label": "SHA Versioning Unused Issue",
    "content": "The commit SHA creates unique release tags (build-abc123def)\nbut users only access '/releases/latest/download' which\nignores the SHA completely. This means:\n- Multiple versioned releases exist but aren't accessible\n- No way for users to download specific versions\n- Old releases become orphaned (tagged but unused)\n- No rollback capability for users",
    "connectedTo": 12,
    "linkLabel": "identifies unused versioning"
  },
  {
    "id": 15,
    "type": "todo",
    "label": "Versioning Convention Explanation",
    "content": "Release tags use format: 'build-{git-commit-sha}'\nThis creates unique releases but doesn't follow semantic\nversioning (v1.0.0). Each push to railway-test creates\na new release with the commit SHA as identifier.",
    "connectedTo": 10,
    "linkLabel": "explains format"
  },
  {
    "id": 16,
    "type": "todo",
    "label": "Download Naming Convention",
    "content": "Artifact names are hardcoded in Downloads.tsx:\n- cochart-js.tar.gz (Node.js version)\n- cochart-win.zip (Windows executable)\n- cochart-mac.tar.gz (macOS binary)\n- cochart-linux.tar.gz (Linux binary)\n- cochart-vscode-plugin-1.0.0.vsix (VS Code)\n- Cochart-IJ-Plugin.zip (IntelliJ)",
    "connectedTo": 13,
    "linkLabel": "defines names"
  },
  {
    "id": 17,
    "type": "todo",
    "label": "GitHub Repo Configuration",
    "content": "Downloads point to 'codechart/codechart' repo via\nVITE_GITHUB_REPO environment variable. This defaults\nto 'codechart/codechart' but can be overridden.\nCurrently no branch-specific download logic exists.",
    "connectedTo": 12,
    "linkLabel": "configures source"
  },
  {
    "id": 18,
    "type": "todo",
    "label": "Latest Release Resolution",
    "content": "GitHub's '/releases/latest/download' always serves\nthe most recent release regardless of branch. If multiple\nbranches create releases, the latest one wins. This can\ncause version confusion in multi-branch development.",
    "connectedTo": 11,
    "linkLabel": "explains behavior"
  }
